```cpp
#include <concepts>

// Predefined concept
template<std::integral T>
void int_only(T x) { /* only integers */ }

// Custom concept
template<typename T>
concept Numeric = std::is_arithmetic_v<T>;

template<Numeric T>
T add(T a, T b) { return a + b; }

// Concept with requires expression
template<typename T>
concept Container = requires(T c) {
    c.begin(); c.end(); c.size();
    typename T::value_type;
};

template<Container C>
void print_all(const C& c) {
    for (const auto& x : c) std::cout << x << " ";
}
```

Concepts replace SFINAE with readable, meaningful constraints. They produce clear error messages when constraints are violated.

```cpp
#include <ranges>

// Ranges — composable lazy sequence operations
auto result = std::views::iota(1, 11)
    | std::views::filter([](int n) { return n % 2 == 0; })
    | std::views::transform([](int n) { return n * n; });

for (int x : result) std::cout << x << " ";  // 4 16 36 64 100

// Ranges are lazy — no intermediate containers!
// Equivalent to: filter even from 1-10, square each
```

Ranges use `|` for composition (like Unix pipes). They are lazy — elements are computed only when iterated. No intermediate `std::vector` allocations needed.

```cpp
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <queue>

// map — sorted key-value (O(log n) operations)
std::map<std::string, int> m;
m["one"] = 1;
m.emplace("two", 2);
m.count("one");    // 1
m.find("one") != m.end();

// unordered_map — hash map (O(1) average)
std::unordered_map<std::string, int> hm;
hm.reserve(100);

// set — sorted unique elements
std::set<int> s = {3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9};  // {1,3,4,5,9}
s.insert(2); s.erase(3);

// priority_queue — heap
std::priority_queue<int> maxpq;                              // max-heap
std::priority_queue<int, std::vector<int>, std::greater<>> minpq;  // min-heap
```

| Container | Ordering | Lookup | Insert/Delete |
|-----------|----------|--------|---------------|
| `map` | sorted | O(log n) | O(log n) |
| `unordered_map` | none | O(1) avg | O(1) avg |
| `set` | sorted unique | O(log n) | O(log n) |
